_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 12
---
order: 12
---
short_label: V.12
---
statement: If any number of magnitudes are proportional, then one of the antecedents is to one of the consequents as the sum of the antecedents is to the sum of the consequents.
---
proof:

Let any number of magnitudes *A, B, C, D, E,* and *F* be proportional, so that *A* is to *B* as *C* is to *D,* and as *E* is to *F.*

I say that *A* is to *B* as the sum of *A, C,* and *E* is to the sum of *B, D,* and *F.*

